      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n`GrowthHYBR.withdraw` always splits the contract’s veNFT into three pieces: the portion that stays in the vault, the user’s share, and the protocol fee. When a user controls 100% of the outstanding gHYBR supply (e.g., the first depositor or the last remaining LP), we obtain:\n\n```solidity\n\nuint256 veBalance = totalAssets();           // 100% of the lock\nuint256 userAmount = hybrAmount - feeAmount; // user’s slice\nuint256 remainingAmount = veBalance - userAmount - feeAmount;\n```\n\nFor the final holder, `remainingAmount` becomes `0`. The code then calls:\n\n```solidity\n\nuint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](3);\namounts[0] = remainingAmount; // 0\namounts[1] = userAmount;\namounts[2] = feeAmount;\nIVotingEscrow(votingEscrow).multiSplit(veTokenId, amounts);\n```\n\nInside `VotingEscrow.multiSplit`, each entry must be strictly positive:\n\n```solidity\nfor (uint i = 0; i < amounts.length; i++) {\n    require(amounts[i] > 0, \"ZW\");\n}\n```\n\nWith a zero remainder the call reverts, aborting the entire withdrawal. The vault burns the user’s gHYBR shares before entering `multiSplit`, so the user loses their shares and remains unable to exit or claim the underlying HYBR ever again. Any trailing penalty/fee accounting is also blocked. This is a permanent, loss-of-funds (final depositor shuts down the pool).\n\n>**NOTE**: A single participant (or the last remaining LP) cannot withdraw their shares; the call deterministically reverts with \"ZW\", leaving funds locked and the accounting (including withdrawal fee) unclaimable.This occurs when user owns 100% of the contract’s veNFT value at withdraw time (typical for the last exiting user). With a non-zero fee, remaining = veBalance - userAmount - fee == 0.\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n- Detect when `remainingAmount == 0` and skip the internal gHYBR slice (e.g., create only two NFTs: user and fee). \n- or guard the 100%-exit path: if shares == totalSupply() (or remaining == 0), handle a dedicated 2-way (user, fee) split; Don’t set veTokenId to a remainder that doesn’t exist. \n- Alternatively, pre-fund a minimal dust amount so `remainingAmount` is never zero.",
      "proofOfConcept": "1. Install dependencies inside `ve33/` (`npm install`), then run:\n   ```bash\n\n   cd ve33\n   forge test --match-path test/C4PoC_GrowthHYBR.t.sol -vvv\n   ```\n   \n2. The PoC (`ve33/test/C4PoC_GrowthHYBR.t.sol`) deploys the full stack, toggles split permissions for gHYBR (mirroring production configuration), deposits 1,000 HYBR as the only participant, advances into the permitted withdrawal window, and calls `withdraw(shares)`.  \n3. The call reverts with `\"ZW\"` from `multiSplit`, demonstrating the final user is unable to exit.\n\n```solidity\n\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.13;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {C4PoCTestbed} from \"./C4PoCTestbed.t.sol\";\nimport {HybraTimeLibrary} from \"../contracts/libraries/HybraTimeLibrary.sol\";\n\ncontract C4PoC_GrowthHYBR is C4PoCTestbed {\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        // Allow gHYBR to call VotingEscrow.multiSplit\n        vm.prank(votingEscrow.team());\n        votingEscrow.toggleSplit(address(gHybr), true);\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        uint256 depositAmount = 1_000 ether;\n\n        // Single participant deposits HYBR into gHYBR (minting gHYBR shares one-to-one).\n        hybr.approve(address(gHybr), depositAmount);\n        gHybr.deposit(depositAmount, address(this));\n\n        // Move into the allowed withdrawal window.\n        uint256 epochStart = HybraTimeLibrary.epochStart(block.timestamp);\n        vm.warp(epochStart + gHybr.head_not_withdraw_time());\n\n        uint256 shares = gHybr.balanceOf(address(this));\n        assertGt(shares, 0, \"no shares minted\");\n\n        // Withdrawing the full share set results in multiSplit receiving a zero slice,\n        // triggering the \"ZW\" revert and permanently locking the last user.\n        vm.expectRevert(bytes(\"ZW\"));\n        gHybr.withdraw(shares);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n```bash\n\n[⠒] Compiling...\nNo files changed, com